Second impressions. Third impressions. And every impression after.

First impressions establish expectations. Subsequent impressions can reinforce, challenge, or completely overturn them.

And sometimes the most revealing thing about a person isn’t how they behave when you first meet them, but how they behave once they no longer feel the need to impress you.

There’s another side, too: people change, but our impressions of them don’t always keep up.

First impressions reveal how someone enters your world. Lasting impressions reveal how they inhabit it.

And perhaps just as importantly, how willing you are to let them become someone different from who you first believed they were.